  "body": "#27 brings in language about busy ports or ports in use by the system.\n\nIt should be noted that a \"busy port\" is not necessarily a `locked` port. Having two processes listen to the same port is very possible, osx, linux and windows. They allow sharing and locking of serialports by processes. \n\nDifferent JavaScript contextes (different tabs, service workers, etc) accessing the same port might be a different situation altogether.\n",
